# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# SQLite — never commit the db file, seed data lives in JSON.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Snapshot artefacts. `*.db` above does NOT cover these: the suffix comes
# after the extension, so `mena_ai.db.snapshot` is not matched by `*.db`.
# These are the temporary VACUUM INTO target and restore staging file
# (backend/src/snapshot), plus the compressed copy produced when seeding App
# Storage by hand — a full production database in every case.
*.db.snapshot
*.db.restore
*.db.gz
*.sqlite.gz

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Environment. The deployment's API credentials live here — Cloudflare Radar,
# Internet Society Pulse and PeeringDB — so this is deliberately a wildcard
# with one explicit exception, rather than a list of the variants anyone has
# happened to create so far. `.env.work`, `.env.replit` and friends are
# exactly the files that would otherwise slip through.
.env*
!.env.example

# Replit. `.replit`, `.replitignore` and `replit.nix` are ours and ARE
# committed — do not add a `.replit*` wildcard here, it would swallow them.
# Everything below is generated by the workspace at runtime.
.upm/
.cache/
.config/
.pythonlibs/
.breakpoints
replit_zip_error_log.txt

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
